message: "If you use this research software, please cite it using this metadata and cite the external mathematical or physical source appropriate to the specific theorem or method used."
title: "Spatiotemporal Observer Mathematics"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Keikha
    given-names: Mahsa
version: 0.47.0
date-released: 2026-09-08
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MahsaKeikha/spatiotemporal-observer-math"
abstract: "Research software and mathematical documentation for dynamically inferred time-dependent subsystem boundaries in stochastic physical systems. The project develops moving world-tube optimization, identifiability, finite-sample covariance certification, physical-time calibration, irregular-grid innovation inference, and deterministic propagation of measurement uncertainty back to the moving-boundary objective. The word observer is operational and the repository does not claim to establish consciousness."
keywords:
  - observer factorization
  - moving subsystem boundary
  - world-tube inference
  - information theory
  - dynamical systems
  - nonstationary Gaussian processes
  - covariance concentration
  - finite-sample inference
  - physical relaxation time
  - innovation whitening
  - integrated information
  - subsystem identification
  - reproducible research
